<Layout title="Privacy Policy - Bin Stores USA" description="Privacy policy for Bin Stores USA: what the site collects, how Google AdSense uses cookies to show ads, and how to change your ad settings.">
  <h1>Privacy Policy</h1>
  <p>Bin Stores USA is a links directory of bin stores in the United States. Each listing has a store name, a city and state, an address when a public source lists one, and a link to a public listing for that store. The site gives no shopping advice and it does not rate, check, or vouch for any store.</p>
  <h2>What this site collects</h2>
  <p>This site collects no personal data itself. It has no accounts, no sign in, no newsletter, and no form that asks for your name or email. It does not sell anything.</p>
  <h2>Ads</h2>
  <p>This site shows ads through Google AdSense. Google, and the companies it works with, may use cookies to show ads that fit what you have looked at. A cookie is a small file a site asks your browser to keep, so it can remember a choice or show ads that fit your interests. You can turn off ads based on your interests, or change what Google knows about your ad interests, at <a href="https://adssettings.google.com/">Google Ad Settings</a>. You can also read how Google uses data in ads at <a href="https://policies.google.com/technologies/ads">Google's advertising privacy page</a>.</p>
  <h2>Links to other sites</h2>
  <p>Each listing links to a store page or a public listing on another site. Those sites have their own privacy rules, and this policy does not cover them.</p>
  <h2>Contact</h2>
  <p>This site lists no email address. If you have a question about a listing, see the <a href="/contact/">Contact page</a>.</p>
  <h2>Changes</h2>
  <p>If this policy changes, the new version will appear on this page.</p>
</Layout>
